# NestJS API — DDD Boundaries

Module layout:

```text
modules/<context>/
  presentation/      # controllers, HTTP DTOs only
  application/       # use cases / application services
  domain/            # entities, VOs, domain services, events, repo ports
  infrastructure/    # Prisma repos, gateways, mappers
  <context>.module.ts
```

## Do

```typescript
// ✅ Controller delegates
@Post(':id/verify')
verify(@Param('id') id: string, @CurrentUser() user: AuthUser) {
  return this.verifyManualPayment.execute({ paymentId: id, actorId: user.id });
}
```

## Don't

```typescript
// ❌ Business rules or Prisma in controllers
@Post(':id/verify')
async verify(@Param('id') id: string) {
  const payment = await this.prisma.payment.findFirst({ where: { id } });
  if (payment.amountKobo < 0) throw new Error('bad');
  payment.status = 'succeeded';
  await this.prisma.payment.update({ where: { id }, data: payment });
}
```

- Domain must not import Nest, Prisma, or Paystack/R2 SDKs.
- Presentation must not inject `PrismaClient` or repositories directly.
- Cross-module writes go through another context’s application facade or domain events — never its Prisma models.
